  "chunk": "tions about the path toward artificial general intelligence. Our findings suggest\nthat current LLMs face substantial challenges in domains requiring adaptive\nreasoning and metacognition, but the scope and implications of the limitations\nof this study warrant further investigation.\nFuture research should address the limitations of this study in several ways.\nFirst, incorporating human player baselines across varying expertise levels would\nprovide context for interpreting model performance and distinguishing between\ntask difficulty and model-specific failures. Second, systematic quantification\nof error types across all conversation logs—including the frequency of repeti-\ntive actions, instances of learning within and across sessions, and categories of\nlogical failures—would move beyond illustrative examples to establish a more\nrigorous understanding of the behaviour. Third, comparative analysis examin-\ning whether the same models exhibit similar metacognitive limitations on games",
